### Printed values are padded

Severity: FAIL (fixable). The step introduction says the check value is the text after `check:`, and that this text starts with the status word.

`format_facts` renders `f"{key + ':':<{width}} {value}"`, with `width` one more than the longest key. The colon is attached to the key. Aligning spaces sit between the colon and the value. On a busy probe the longest key is longer than `check`, so the text after `check:` is spaces and then `swapped ...`. That text does not start with `swapped`. The same spaces sit after `warehouse:` and `backup:`, so a comparison of the raw tail to `busy` or `absent` fails the same way.

Say the value is the field after those spaces. The check value starts with the status word. The warehouse value `busy` and the backup value `absent` are that field.

